{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Teach me</b> — in seeing by way of prophecy that HaShem answers him, and he pleads to arrange for himself causes and dispositions, to add the fear of Your name." "<b>And the word יחד</b> — from the root of יחיד, or חבר from the root of יחד."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 86, :notes {0 "Reading והוא מתחנן as 'and he pleads,' referring to the psalmist; the syntax is compressed and the referent of יענהו is resolved as the supplicant being answered by HaShem."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:11.196223547Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}